.TH HASHCHECK 1 "November 2026" "revision" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hashcheck \- Hashcat wrapper with conservative hash format detection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hashcheck-rc
.B -i HASH | -f FILE
.B -c CONFIG
.RB [ --mode " NUMBER"]
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs Hashcat with a configured wordlist. Only selected structured hash formats are identified automatically. Raw hexadecimal digests are ambiguous and require an explicit mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -i HASH
Supply one hash.
.TP
.B -f FILE
Read the first whitespace-delimited token from a file.
.TP
.B -c CONFIG
Read a JSON configuration with hashcat_path and wordlist strings.
.TP
.B --mode NUMBER
Select the Hashcat mode explicitly.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the planned arguments without executing Hashcat.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success, nonzero on invalid input or execution failure.
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/rcallaby/hashcheck/issues
